course: dictionary
lesson: 3531
title: Feathers, a word with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A feather is one of the light, soft parts that cover a bird's body. In «Penguins also keep warm with a thick layer of fat and tightly packed waterproof feathers», the clues warm and waterproof tell you what feathers do for a penguin.
explain: Feather can also be a verb. To feather a nest means to make it soft. A nest is a home for eggs and chicks, so the words around feather suggest it is about making something cosy.
explain: Read «light as a feather». This is a phrase, not a real feather. It means very light. When a word appears in a phrase, check the words around it before you decide what it means.
fact: Feather is a noun: one feather, or more than one feather.
fact: A feather is one of the light, soft parts that cover a bird's body.
fact: Feathers keep birds warm and dry and help them fly.
fact: «Light as a feather» means very light.
fact: To «feather a nest» means to make it soft.
exercise: «Penguins also keep warm with a thick layer of fat and tightly packed waterproof feathers.» Apart from fat, what keeps penguins warm? | Their beaks | *Feathers | Sunshine | Ice
exercise: «Birds bathe to keep their feathers clean and working well.» Why do birds bathe? | To stop them from flying | To make their feathers longer | *To keep their feathers clean and working well | To turn their feathers blue
exercise: What does «light as a feather» mean? | Very soft and fluffy like a pillow | Very heavy | *Very light | Very wet
test: In «Feathers keep birds warm and dry and help them fly», what jobs do feathers do? | *Keep birds warm and dry, and help them fly | Help birds swim faster than fish | Make birds sing loudly | Turn birds into other colours
test: In the phrase «to feather a nest», what does feather mean? | To break it | To paint it | *To make it soft | To hide it from view
exam: On the Moon in 1971, an astronaut dropped a hammer and a feather; what happened to them? | The feather floated up and the hammer sank | They fell at different speeds | The hammer bounced and the feather fell | *They landed together
